K-Means Clustering Lab
Purpose

This lab applies the K-Means clustering algorithm to group customer location data into three clusters using Euclidean distance.

Key Insights

The algorithm converged to three clusters:

Cluster 1: P1, Q1, R2 → (4.667, 10.667)
Cluster 2: P3, Q2, Q3 → (8, 4)
Cluster 3: P2, R1 → (2.5, 4.5)

The results show that points located closer together are grouped into the same cluster.

Challenges and Decisions

The main challenge was calculating distances and updating cluster centers across multiple iterations. R2 had an equal distance to two initial centers, so it was assigned to Cluster 1 as a tie-breaking decision. The algorithm was repeated until the cluster centers stopped changing.